message: "If you use this test, its ledger or its results, please cite the repository."
title: "Was the Great Pyramid a sulfuric-acid plant? A quantitative test"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jannatabaadi
    given-names: MHadi
repository-code: "https://github.com/hadijannat/pyramid-acid-plant-test"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-12"
keywords:
  - Great Pyramid
  - Giza
  - hypothesis testing
  - reproducible research
  - Mie scattering
  - FDTD
  - hydraulics
  - sulfuric acid
abstract: >-
  A neutral, quantitative and reproducible test of the "Land of Chem" hypothesis that the
  Great Pyramid of Giza ran as a sulfuric-acid plant. The 71 claims of the hypothesis are
  written down as stated, each with a criterion fixed before computation; every physical
  number comes from one sourced ledger; hand calculations, the survey record, a register
  of the documentary evidence, reduced models of flow, chemistry and conduction, and two
  full-wave field solvers decide the claims, and every result regenerates from the ledger.
